#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:4
msgid "Understanding the Local Version Counter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:7
msgid "Description"
msgstr "描述"

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:9
msgid ""
"Changes to files are tracked by so called *version vectors*, which can be "
"used to understand a file's provenance in terms of who changed it after "
"receiving a copy from whom, etc. However, for other purposes we just need to "
"know which files have changed since a certain point in time. For example "
"this is used to determine which files to send information about when "
"connecting to a device that we have already exchanged some index information "
"with at an earlier time. For this purpose we have the *local version "
"counter*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:17
msgid ""
"Conceptually it is an ever increasing integer kept for each folder by each "
"device. Each time a change is made to the index information of an item (file "
"or directory), that item is tagged with the current value of the local "
"version counter, and the counter is increased."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:23
msgid "Principal of Operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:25
msgid ""
"Assume that the starting value of the counter is ``0``. The next change that "
"happens will be assigned local version ``1``. Local scanning reveals the "
"presence of three new files, ``foo``, ``bar`` and ``baz``. When ``foo`` is "
"discovered, it's index entry gets assigned local version ``1`` and the "
"counter is increased. Likewise ``bar`` gets ``2`` and ``baz`` gets ``3``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:32 ../../../draft/localver.rst:43
msgid "File"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:32 ../../../draft/localver.rst:43
msgid "Local Version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:34 ../../../draft/localver.rst:45
msgid "foo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:34 ../../../draft/localver.rst:45
msgid "1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:35 ../../../draft/localver.rst:46
msgid "bar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:35
msgid "2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:36 ../../../draft/localver.rst:47
msgid "baz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:36 ../../../draft/localver.rst:47
msgid "3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:39
msgid ""
"The next change to happen will be assigned the value ``4``. If the file "
"``bar`` is updated, the index will look like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:46
msgid "4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:50
msgid ""
"If we had already given the first index above to another device, and they "
"tell us that they see a maximum local version value of ``3``, then we know "
"that we only need to send them information about entries with local version "
"number ``4`` or higher -- in this case the entry for ``bar``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:56
msgid "Implementation Details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:58
msgid ""
"In actual operation, the local version is assigned from the current "
"timestamp in Unix epoch nanoseconds, potentially incremented in case of "
"multiple changes happening during the same clock nanosecond. This guarantees "
"that local version numbers are monotonically increasing even in the case of "
"losing the local index database, and allows for detecting that case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:64
msgid ""
"During the initial protocol handshake (the \"Cluster Configuration\" "
"message) each device sends the maximum known local version number (per "
"folder) to the other device. That device can then send index information "
"based on the difference between the received maximum local version number "
"and the current local version counter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:70
msgid ""
"If the received maximum local version is lower than the *minimum* local "
"version number in our index, the other device is fully out of date with our "
"index information or a database reset has occurred. We send a *full index* "
"(\"Index message\" followed by one or more \"Index Update\" messages)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:75
msgid ""
"If the received maximum local version number is lower than the *maximum* "
"local version number in our index, the other device is missing some of our "
"index information. We send an *incremental index* (\"Index Update\" messages "
"only) containing all index entries with higher local version numbers than "
"the received maximum."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/localver.rst:81
msgid ""
"If the received maximum local version number is equal to the maximum local "
"version number in our index, the other device is fully up to date with our "
"index information."
msgstr ""
